DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260520T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260520T210000
SUMMARY:Wednesday night Bent Creek
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nHard Times Trailhead near Lake Pow
 hatan Rec Area\nRSVP's don't open until 6PM Sunday night.\nWeather: Looks 
 like rain predicted\, will know more by Tuesday or Wednesday early\, and w
 ill let everyone know the details then.\nI did this hike series for many y
 ears before 2022\, but I did it as a high-speed hike\, and I am now doing 
 it as a moderate speed hike. This is a numbers limited event and I expect 
 people who sign-up to show up. Late cancellations\, and those that don't s
 how up are bumping other interested hikers\, and they will not be allowed 
 on future hikes.\nIf all goes well\, I will try to post a hike most weeks\
 , and for days Tue or Wed\, distance\, and start location\, like switching
  between Hard Times trail-head and Bent Creek River Park\, may change.\nTh
 e current route is about 5.5 miles.\nPlease folks\, this is intended as a 
 moderate paced hike\, and we'd like all attendees to keep up with the hike
  leader(s). This hike is intended as a workout hike for people to get in c
 ondition to do weekend hikes.\nModerate paced means 22-24 min miles\, or 2
  ½ mph.\nAs such\, we do not take breaks\, take in views\, or snap photos
  along the way. Please make sure you're able to keep up with the group. Th
 is hike has always served as a good chance to get exercise during the week
 \, meet new people\, and create interest for weekend enjoyment hikes. It's
  a great introduction to the AHG family.\nNo need to RSVP "No" or "not att
 ending" unless changing from a "Yes."\nPlease read the full description be
 fore RSVPing\, and only sign up if you are sure you can go. Thanks in adva
 nce for keeping your RSVP up-to-date and not being a last-minute cancellat
 ion or no-show. This is an ongoing issue with Meetups and often keeps peop
 le on waitlists from being able to attend our hikes.\nHard Times Trailhead
  near Lake Powhatan Rec Area\nFollow signs off of Brevard Rd (Rt 191) to L
 ake Powhatan Rec Area. The road is Bent Creek Ranch Rd. to Wesley Branch R
 d. Follow signs to Lake Powhatan until you come to Hard Times Trailhead on
  your left\, 2.5 miles. It is very clearly marked. Parking is very limited
  at the trailhead but there’s a paved pull-off just before the Hard Time
 s trailhead and more parking just beyond at the Ledford Branch trailhead. 
 We will access Bent Creek forest by way of Hard Times Trail and do some co
 mbination of loop and out and back.\nArrive at the trailhead BY 6:00. Beca
 use it is a weeknight hike\, we are unable to wait for latecomers\, fighti
 ng daylight.\n\\*\\*\\*If you are running behind\, please post a comment o
 n this Meetup page by 5:45 pm. There is no cell service at the parking lot
 \, so if we don't have any advance notice of you running late by 5:45\, we
  can't get any notifications at the trailhead and we will not wait for you
 .\nWe start the hike at 6:00\, rarely do we get much later than that.\n•
  Wear closed-toed footwear appropriate for hiking. The trail will consist 
 of dirt\, rocks\, roots\, mud and mulch.\n• Bring plenty of water.\n• 
 Bring rain gear if a chance of rain is in the forecast.\nHeadlamps suggest
 ed\n• Dogs on leashes the whole time are welcome. This is an active moun
 tain bike area and it can get messy with dogs running loose among hikers a
 nd mountain bikers.\nPlease make sure to keep your RSVP up-to-date. You do
 n't want to be "that person" who cancels last minute or no-shows and keeps
  someone from joining in if there's a waitlist. Thanks for your considerat
 ion - it is appreciated!\nFeel free to post questions not covered in this 
 description in the comments section.\nThanks - we'll see you on the trail!
 \nDisclaimer and Release of Liability:\nThis activity involves hiking on c
 ity streets that may have traffic and/or natural trails with roots\, rocks
 \, and steep sections. Participants are responsible for their safety on st
 reets and trails. The organizer of this trip is a volunteer and not a prof
 essional guide. The function of the organizer is only to organize this tri
 p. If you sign up or participate in this event you acknowledge that you fr
 eely and voluntarily agree to assume all risks of injuries\, illnesses\, a
 nd damages arising from\, as a result of\, and associated with this event.
  In addition\, you acknowledge that you agree to the Meetup terms: [https:
 //www.meetup.com/terms](https://www.meetup.com/terms)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/314822961
 /
